        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-13T19:13:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We decided to hide this quite a while ago. Otherwise, we would need to generate the callback info structs in C++ which would have callback function types with C types. It\u0027s doable, but IMO this is a lot more ergonomic, and if users want to do stuff with the actual members, they can work in C instead of C++. The whole point of the C++ bindings is to make it easier and more idiomatic to C++.",
      "parentUuid": "5ee50834_64eb8cf1",
      "revId": "965a4fd9c1186c6e9cbd56028714cfc4ba27debe",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
